## Root cause

`Context.FileAttachment` (context.go) built the ASCII `Content-Disposition` header by raw string concatenation:

```go
c.Writer.Header().Set("Content-Disposition", `attachment; filename="`+filename+`"`)
```

The filename was never escaped, so a filename containing `"` or `\` (e.g. `"new\filename".go"`) broke out of the quoted-string and produced a malformed/incorrect header. The repository contains **no** escaping helper at all (`grep -rn 'escapeQuotes\|quoteEscaper'` over the whole tree returned nothing; `utils.go` has only `isASCII`), so the helper the upstream code relies on had been removed. The non-ASCII branch (`filename*=UTF-8''` + `url.QueryEscape`) was already correct and matches the existing `TestContextRenderUTF8Attachment`, so it was left untouched.

